      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:40:3",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ الرَّجُلِ عَلَيْهِ دَيْنٌ يَسْتَقْرِضُ وَ يَحُجُّ قَالَ إِنْ كَانَ لَهُ وَجْهٌ فِي مَالٍ فَلَا بَأْسَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Ali Bin Al Hakam, from Abdul Malik Bin Utba who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> about the man upon whom are debts; can he borrow and perform Hajj?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘If there was for him a (replacement) asset in wealth, so there is no problem’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Ali ibn al-Hakam from ‘Abd al-Malik ibn ‘Utbah who has said the following: “I once asked abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who owes a loan already; if he can borrow for al-Hajj expenses. He (the Imam) said, ‘It is not harmful if he has an asset that can pay off the loan.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
